  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and men workers and enterprises benefit from safe and healthy workplaces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this Country Programme Outcome, the ILO will strengthen national and state capacities to realise safe and healthy working environments in the context of India&apos;s new Occupational Safety, Health and Working Conditions Rules effective from April 2026. Technical support to the Ministry of Labour and Employment and selected states will facilitate implementation of the new regulatory framework and development of state OSH profiles, while reinforcing alignment with up-to-date international OSH standards and supporting progress towards ratification of key OSH Conventions.

In sectors linked to trade and investment priorities including ship recycling under the Hong Kong Convention, shrimp processing, textiles and garments, agriculture, construction and the platform economy the ILO will promote risk-based and prevention-focused approaches. This includes strengthening OSH systems in FTA-linked sectors, integrating heat stress into policies and programmes, and supporting tripartite capacity-building and roadmap development. Together, these measures aim to improve institutional coordination, sector-level compliance and reporting, and protection of workers in both formal and informal segments of India&apos;s evolving economy.</narrative>
  </description>
